00:26:27.953 --> 00:26:29.287
which is what human
beings always do.

00:26:29.287 --> 00:26:30.488
Human beings are sinful.

00:26:30.488 --> 00:26:31.823
Human beings can be evil.

00:26:31.823 --> 00:26:33.625 align:start size:88% position:13%
Human beings do horrible
things to each other.

00:26:33.625 --> 00:26:34.993
And so the story
of American history

00:26:34.993 --> 00:26:36.895
is us seeking to live
up to those principles

00:26:36.895 --> 00:26:39.264 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then failing and then
striving and then succeeding.

00:26:39.264 --> 00:26:41.833 align:start position:0%
And that's a great story because
that's a story of triumph

00:26:41.833 --> 00:26:43.802
and it means that we're all
part of the same history.

00:26:43.802 --> 00:26:45.503
Even if we're part of
a victimized group,

00:26:45.503 --> 00:26:46.805 align:start size:84% position:16%
then we're the
heroes of the story,

00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:49.007
because we overcame
that victimization

00:26:49.007 --> 00:26:52.277
to become part of this great
chain that is the United States

00:26:52.277 --> 00:26:54.479
to claim our share of the
American dream, right?

00:26:54.479 --> 00:26:56.181
And I'm not the one saying this,

00:26:56.181 --> 00:26:57.616
Frederick Douglas
was saying this

00:26:57.616 --> 00:26:59.951
as a former freed slave in 1852,

00:26:59.951 --> 00:27:01.920 align:start size:97% position:3%
he was talking about how
July 4th doesn't include us,

00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:03.455
but it should include us

00:27:03.455 --> 00:27:05.123
because Independence Day was
meant to apply to everyone.

00:27:05.123 --> 00:27:07.025
So are you gonna live up
to your promises or not?

00:27:07.025 --> 00:27:08.727
This is Martin Luther
King's promissory note.

00:27:08.727 --> 00:27:10.462
The idea that work
here to make good

00:27:10.462 --> 00:27:13.064
on the check that you
signed us in 1776.

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:15.567 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so American history
is the story of us

00:27:15.567 --> 00:27:17.268
trying to fulfill
those principles

00:27:17.268 --> 00:27:18.570
and getting better and better

00:27:18.570 --> 00:27:19.938 align:start size:88% position:13%
and extending those
principles to a broader

00:27:19.938 --> 00:27:21.439
and broader group of people,

00:27:21.439 --> 00:27:22.941
which is a story of triumph.

00:27:22.941 --> 00:27:24.509
And not just extend those
principles internally,

00:27:24.509 --> 00:27:26.011 align:start size:97% position:3%
but also extend those
principles around the world.

00:27:26.011 --> 00:27:27.245
The idea of free markets

00:27:27.245 --> 00:27:29.748
and ownership of your
own means of production

00:27:29.748 --> 00:27:31.883 align:start size:88% position:13%
and extending this
around the world to free

00:27:31.883 --> 00:27:34.052
billions of people from
enslavement and poverty,

00:27:34.052 --> 00:27:36.688
the idea of an America that
frees billions of people

00:27:36.688 --> 00:27:38.056
from abject tyranny, right?

00:27:38.056 --> 00:27:39.791 align:start size:81% position:19%
That's an amazing,
amazing story.

00:27:39.791 --> 00:27:41.626 align:start size:88% position:13%
So the story of America
is that America,

00:27:41.626 --> 00:27:44.029 align:start size:84% position:16%
President Trump
once, a slogan aired,

00:27:44.029 --> 00:27:45.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm gonna make
America great again.

00:27:45.196 --> 00:27:46.464
But the idea of American history

00:27:46.464 --> 00:27:48.333
is that America always
had great principals,

00:27:48.333 --> 00:27:49.334
but people are not always great.

00:27:49.334 --> 00:27:50.535
So America was always great

00:27:50.535 --> 00:27:51.770 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you think of
America as an idea.

00:27:51.770 --> 00:27:53.271
If you think of America
as a set of Americans,

00:27:53.271 --> 00:27:55.373
there were some who sucked
and some who were great.

00:27:55.373 --> 00:27:57.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the idea is that
America was always great,

00:27:57.642 --> 00:27:59.144
it was great from inception,

00:27:59.144 --> 00:28:01.479
it just didn't live up to
its own founding creed.

00:28:01.479 --> 00:28:02.881
And then finally,

00:28:02.881 --> 00:28:04.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's the idea of a culture
that ties us together.

00:28:04.382 --> 00:28:05.950
And this doesn't mean that
we watch the same TV shows,

00:28:05.950 --> 00:28:08.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
it means that we speak
sort of the same language.

00:28:08.520 --> 00:28:11.189
That when I say right, you
know inherently what I mean.

00:28:11.189 --> 00:28:13.725
When I say free speech, we
both immediately flash to,

00:28:13.725 --> 00:28:15.193
okay, that means I
can say what I want.

00:28:15.193 --> 00:28:17.395 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I say that there's
freedom of association means,

00:28:17.395 --> 00:28:18.797
okay, it means I get to
hang out with the person

00:28:18.797 --> 00:28:19.798
I want to hang out with.

00:28:19.798 --> 00:28:21.566
If we say freedom of religion,

00:28:21.566 --> 00:28:23.968
it means I get to worship
in the way that I want.

00:28:23.968 --> 00:28:26.771
These are just clear cut
things that we agree on,

00:28:26.771 --> 00:28:28.006
ways that we discuss the world

00:28:28.006 --> 00:28:29.240
and a culture of rights,

00:28:29.240 --> 00:28:30.775
not just legal rights
that are enshrined,

00:28:30.775 --> 00:28:32.043
a culture of rights means

00:28:32.043 --> 00:28:33.712
that even outside the
bounds of government,

00:28:33.712 --> 00:28:35.847
we should respect
each other enough

00:28:35.847 --> 00:28:37.515
to acknowledge that we're
gonna disagree sometimes.

00:28:37.515 --> 00:28:38.850
This is where we get
into cancel culture,

00:28:38.850 --> 00:28:40.652
because the idea is that,

00:28:40.652 --> 00:28:41.853 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you'll hear
this from the left.

00:28:41.853 --> 00:28:44.422 align:start size:88% position:13%
well, when the New York
Times outs somebody

00:28:44.422 --> 00:28:47.092 align:start size:97% position:3%
or when the Atlantic fires
Kevin Williamson or something,

00:28:47.092 --> 00:28:49.327 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's not the
government doing it.

00:28:49.327 --> 00:28:50.528 align:start size:81% position:19%
So what are you
complaining about?

00:28:50.528 --> 00:28:51.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's just the
free market at work.

00:28:51.629 --> 00:28:52.731
That's true, that's true.

00:28:52.731 --> 00:28:53.665
It's not the government,

00:28:53.665 --> 00:28:55.200
but that only goes so far.

00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:56.134
If we don't have a culture
where we actually respect

00:28:56.134 --> 00:28:57.736
each other's ability to speak,

00:28:57.736 --> 00:29:00.805 align:start size:97% position:3%
then culture always precedes
what happens in law.

00:29:00.805 --> 00:29:03.241
It's a pretty short leap
from the entire culture

00:29:03.241 --> 00:29:04.876
says a view is out of balance

00:29:04.876 --> 00:29:08.246 align:start size:88% position:13%
to let's make that view
illegal eventually.

00:29:08.246 --> 00:29:09.514
Now that doesn't mean all views

00:29:09.514 --> 00:29:11.082 align:start size:81% position:19%
have to be held
in equal respects.

00:29:11.082 --> 00:29:12.751
Doesn't mean there's no such
thing as an Overton window.

00:29:12.751 --> 00:29:14.252
Of course there is
an Overton window,

00:29:14.252 --> 00:29:15.954
but it does mean that you
have to have enough respect

00:29:15.954 --> 00:29:17.689
for your neighbor to
say, listen, we're
allowed to disagree.

00:29:17.689 --> 00:29:19.290
And our rights mean
that you're allowed

00:29:19.290 --> 00:29:20.792
to misuse that right

00:29:20.792 --> 00:29:21.993
even I don't like the way
you're using that right.

00:29:21.993 --> 00:29:23.895 align:start size:88% position:13%
The way to overcome your
misuse of that right

00:29:23.895 --> 00:29:27.031
is by using my rights,
my right to free speech,

00:29:27.031 --> 00:29:29.667
to gather a group people
who disagree with you,

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.136
and then we can win.

00:29:31.136 --> 00:29:33.538
Then we can convince you and
