they lost the
election this time,

01:15:45.807 --> 01:15:47.576
but they have won everything.

01:15:47.576 --> 01:15:51.146
They demolished the
democratic party.

01:15:51.146 --> 01:15:53.615
You can't point to me, but
please do if you can, Ben,

01:15:53.615 --> 01:15:56.718
where is any decent Democrat?

01:15:56.718 --> 01:15:57.819
Where is JFK?

01:15:57.819 --> 01:15:59.288
Where's Daniel Patrick Moynihan?

01:15:59.288 --> 01:16:00.556
Where is any-

01:16:00.556 --> 01:16:02.090
- There are few and
far between, I mean,

01:16:02.090 --> 01:16:04.159
I think that they've tried
to ask them in primaries,

01:16:04.159 --> 01:16:05.727
Nancy Pelosi endorsed Ilhan Omar

01:16:05.727 --> 01:16:07.095
for reelection the other day.

01:16:07.095 --> 01:16:09.831
I mean, this is not
any great shock.

01:16:09.831 --> 01:16:11.066
I think you're right.

01:16:11.066 --> 01:16:12.367 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think they've captured
the democratic party.

01:16:12.367 --> 01:16:13.602
I think more than anything,

01:16:13.602 --> 01:16:15.571 align:start size:84% position:16%
the right focused
on the wrong things.

01:16:15.571 --> 01:16:17.539
So I talk in the
book about culture,

01:16:17.539 --> 01:16:20.075
the right speak more
broadly about culture,

01:16:20.075 --> 01:16:23.378 align:start size:84% position:16%
the right never
had the wherewithal

01:16:23.378 --> 01:16:25.280
to compete in the cultural space

01:16:25.280 --> 01:16:27.115
or in the educational space.

01:16:27.115 --> 01:16:28.850
And so they basically seeded
the ground and then they said,

01:16:28.850 --> 01:16:30.352
you know what, we'll win
it back at the ballot box.

01:16:30.352 --> 01:16:31.987
Right, we'll elect Republicans.

01:16:31.987 --> 01:16:34.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
Republicans had been
elected in several recent

01:16:34.656 --> 01:16:38.093 align:start size:88% position:13%
presidential elections,
2000, 2004, 2016.

01:16:39.494 --> 01:16:42.698
They held Congress all
the way from 1994 to 2006

01:16:42.698 --> 01:16:45.434
and then they held that
again from 2010 to 2018.

01:16:45.434 --> 01:16:48.570
They held the Senate for
wide stretches of that time

01:16:48.570 --> 01:16:50.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the country continued
to move to the left.

01:16:50.939 --> 01:16:52.641 align:start size:97% position:3%
The country continued to move
to the left in every way.

01:16:52.641 --> 01:16:54.476 align:start position:0%
And that is because the
institutions of popular culture

01:16:54.476 --> 01:16:56.078
and the media were
totally taken over.

01:16:56.078 --> 01:16:58.280 align:start size:97% position:3%
The great lie that
Republicans kept banking on

01:16:58.280 --> 01:17:00.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
is that reality would
eventually kick in for folks.

01:17:00.782 --> 01:17:02.317
The idea was, and I know this

01:17:02.317 --> 01:17:04.753
because I've been operating
on campuses for a long time.

01:17:04.753 --> 01:17:06.521
- You also wrote
a book about it.

01:17:06.521 --> 01:17:08.490
- Yeah, that's true.

01:17:08.490 --> 01:17:09.891
But I mean, just from
operating on campuses,

01:17:09.891 --> 01:17:11.360
one of the great things
that would happen is

01:17:11.360 --> 01:17:13.161
my very first book, which
I wrote when I was 19,

01:17:13.161 --> 01:17:15.897
was about liberal bias
on college campuses.

01:17:15.897 --> 01:17:19.601
And one of the most frequent
questions I got was, well,

01:17:19.601 --> 01:17:21.269 align:start size:88% position:13%
